    "html": "<p>An ideal gas undergoes a reversible isothermal expansion at a temperature of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\\text{ K}\"></span>. During the expansion, the gas performs <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1200\\text{ J}\"></span> of work on its surroundings. What is the change in the entropy of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0\\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span>.</p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0\\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span>.</p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.33\\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span>.</p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.8 \\times 10^5\\text{ J K}^{-1}\"></span>.</p></li></ol>"
